WEBVTT

00:00:00.558 --> 00:00:04.178
Space-X is a self-evolving framework for spatial reasoning.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:09.092
Its central idea is simple: better reasoning comes from connecting evidence, not

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:10.488
merely from adding tools.

00:00:11.891 --> 00:00:17.060
Tool-augmented agents can miss a crucial observation, mix object identities or

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.667
reference frames, and decide before the evidence is complete.

00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:24.788
A correct tool output only becomes useful when it supports the question being

00:00:24.788 --> 00:00:25.367
asked.

00:00:26.784 --> 00:00:30.548
An execution agent constructs an evidence chain for each task.

00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:35.750
A control agent studies execution traces and evaluation feedback, then improves the

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.966
surrounding harness.

00:00:37.205 --> 00:00:42.002
Tools, interfaces, skills, memory, and decision rules evolve together.

00:00:43.391 --> 00:00:45.569
The question determines what evidence is needed.

00:00:45.807 --> 00:00:49.162
Source-aware tools acquire observations and geometry.

00:00:49.401 --> 00:00:54.317
The harness binds results to objects, sources, and reference frames, then checks

00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:56.602
whether the key claims have sufficient support.

00:00:56.829 --> 00:00:59.403
Every decision stays connected to its evidence.

00:01:00.796 --> 00:01:04.920
Consider the distance between the closest surfaces of a stool and a toilet.

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:09.955
Segmentation identifies the objects, and depth supplies geometry from the same

00:01:09.955 --> 00:01:10.642
source.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.931
The harness selects the requested surface-to-surface measurement and produces an

00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:17.240
answer of zero point eight six meters.

00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:23.102
A mural is visible in one image, but the question refers to a different camera.

00:01:23.341 --> 00:01:27.932
Space-X associates the target with shared geometry and transforms it into the

00:01:27.932 --> 00:01:29.352
requested camera frame.

00:01:29.591 --> 00:01:33.906
The resulting relation is behind, rather than an answer based on image position

00:01:33.906 --> 00:01:34.436
alone.

00:01:35.922 --> 00:01:40.573
Five role-specific memories preserve the working state, observations, spatial

00:01:40.573 --> 00:01:44.361
relations, execution history, and reusable procedures.

00:01:44.648 --> 00:01:48.784
For counting, repeated sightings are associated with physical instances.

00:01:49.011 --> 00:01:53.783
In this example, eight accepted sightings support two monitors, rather than eight

00:01:53.783 --> 00:01:54.986
separate objects.

00:01:56.379 --> 00:02:01.584
Across ViewSpatial, SPAR, MMSI, and VSI, all four base models

00:02:01.584 --> 00:02:03.100
improve with Space-X.

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:08.555
For GPT-6-sol, ViewSpatial rises from fifty-three point one nine to

00:02:08.555 --> 00:02:10.492
seventy-nine point nine nine.

00:02:10.803 --> 00:02:16.139
For Gemini Flash, VSI rises from fifty-three point zero nine to sixty-six

00:02:16.139 --> 00:02:19.122
point four two, using ten initial frames.

00:02:20.504 --> 00:02:23.307
The ablation makes the central insight concrete.

00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:28.593
On ViewSpatial, evolving tools alone reaches sixty-eight point one five, while

00:02:28.593 --> 00:02:33.343
jointly evolving tools and evidence rules reaches seventy-nine point nine nine.

00:02:33.581 --> 00:02:36.900
The key is to make different tool outputs work together as evidence.

00:02:38.308 --> 00:02:42.347
The development sequence contains five hundred and seventy-five optimization

00:02:42.347 --> 00:02:44.596
candidates across five categories.

00:02:44.823 --> 00:02:50.351
As tools, skills, memory, evidence links, and control improve together, spatial

00:02:50.351 --> 00:02:51.988
reasoning performance increases.

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:54.824
Capabilities accumulate through their connections.

00:02:56.225 --> 00:02:58.642
The harness also transfers across models.

00:02:58.881 --> 00:03:03.929
With X-SFT, the target model continues self-evolution from the inherited

00:03:03.929 --> 00:03:06.960
structure, reusing the original development data.

00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:12.102
Fifteen iterations further improve all three target models, providing a lower-cost

00:03:12.102 --> 00:03:14.231
route than rebuilding from scratch.

00:03:15.641 --> 00:03:20.799
Space-X turns fragmented spatial clues into traceable, derivable answers.

00:03:21.026 --> 00:03:25.161
Its contribution is not a larger collection of settings, but a harness whose

00:03:25.161 --> 00:03:27.194
components learn to work together.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:30.811
